WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.230
Bolivia and Chile are the 50 Cent and Kanye
West of Latin America.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.209
Now, it is true, they share a border.

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:16.930
But other than that, they couldn’t be more
different.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.480
Bolivia is one of the poorest countries on
the whole continent, while Chile is among

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.680
the wealthiest.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.000
Bolivia is a paragon of the so-called indigenous
socialism, while Chile is known as the Mordor

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.630
of neo-liberalism.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:33.650
And as if this was not enough, the two countries
are involved in seemingly never-ending territorial

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:34.870
disputes with each.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.340
Nonetheless, now, there is one thing this
two countries have in common.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.220
Yes, dear viewer... we are talking about WHITE
GOLD.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.220
Wait…

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:52.339
no, I’m not talking about that sort of white
gold.

00:00:52.339 --> 00:00:54.780
I’m talking about LITHIUM.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.070
Lithium is the metal used for manufacturing
the batteries that power your cell phone,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:02.879
your laptop and those electric cars that,
eventually, might flood our roads and highways.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:04.339
They call it “the new oil.”

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:06.750
It’s the lightest metal on the periodic
table.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.100
It’s value has been multiplied by 10 in
the last two decades alone.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.750
And it’s demand doesn’t stop growing.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.461
Between 60 and 80% of the world’s known
reserves are in an area called the LITHIUM

00:01:20.461 --> 00:01:21.530
TRIANGLE.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.250
This is an area that covers parts of Argentina,
Bolivia and Chile.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.499
In these countries, lithium is abundant and
easy to extract.

00:01:28.499 --> 00:01:44.259
In other words, this part of the planet might
soon become the new Saudi Arabia.

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:47.520
Among those three countries, Bolivia is the
luckiest one.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.820
The so-called SALAR DE UYUNI holds 2 or 3
times more lithium reserves than the mines

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.219
in Argentina or Chile.

00:01:54.219 --> 00:01:57.320
On the other hand, Chile already has a world
class mining industry.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.359
However, despite these reserves Bolivia is
exporting less lithium than the other two

00:02:01.359 --> 00:02:02.389
countries.

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:05.819
And Chile might actually soon be out of this
new “white gold rush”.

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:10.250
In fact, Argentina is the nation that is getting
the most attention from international investors.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.190
So today’s question has to be...

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.150
What’s going on in Bolivia?

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.970
Why is no one exploiting their lithium resources?

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.010
And why is Chile following suit?

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.310
Today, we are going to answer all of those
questions.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:26.060
But before… let’s take a look at the history.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.810
A NEW POTOSI?

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.920
If you’ve been subscribed to VisualPolitik
for a long time, you already know that having

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.120
natural resources doesn’t mean you are rich.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.740
Bolivia is a clear example of this.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:44.970
This country has all the natural wealth you
can imagine: lithium, silver, natural gas…

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.150
Nevertheless, this is one of the poorest countries
in all of South America.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:54.230
The silver mines of Potosi were the site of
war for the Spanish crown during the 16th

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.820
and 17th centuries.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:02.480
In fact, Spaniards still say ‘this is worth
a “POTOSI”’ meaning that something is

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.730
too expensive...

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:07.680
But the native Bolivians didn’t reap the
benefits of that silver wealth and millions

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.310
died under the extreme working conditions.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:15.260
This is why it is understandable that the
Government of Evo Morales is so reluctant

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:19.530
to allow foreign companies to get into the
country and extract the lithium.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:27.010
Besides, let’s be honest… the real business
here is not in the raw materials but in the

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.910
industry that comes afterwards.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:32.400
For a better understanding of this, while
we make this video, a metric ton of lithium

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.960
costs around $9,000 on the international market.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.180
But if we take that raw lithium and we turn
it into batteries for mobile phones, we can

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:45.970
turn that lithium into a value of somewhere
between $1.5M and $5M.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:49.940
Of course, this is just a rough estimated
and there lots of things that should be considered

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:50.940
here.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.380
But it can help to look at a comparison.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:59.670
Indeed it can explain this sort of news:
‘President Evo Morales opened, in 2013,

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:07.620
the first plant of lithium carbonate and,
in February 2014, the first factory of ion-lithium

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.620
batteries manufacturing.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:09.620
But that is not all...

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.750
In Bolivia, Lithium is nationalized.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:15.960
This means that, if you are a private mining
company and you want to work on Bolivian soil,

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:19.970
you must partner with the government and start
a new company which will be owned, partly,

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:21.009
by the government.

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:25.180
This new company can get paid for their service
of building the mine, setting up the machinery,

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.719
extracting the lithium etc…

00:04:26.719 --> 00:04:34.139
BUT the lithium they extract belongs to the
government - they have no right to sell it.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:36.449
So, now you might be wondering…

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:40.389
Why does Bolivia need foreign companies to
exploit their own wealth?

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:42.560
Can’t they do it themselves?

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.110
Well, the answer is NO.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:48.900
Modern-day mining has nothing to do with the
image you probably have in your mind of a

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.930
guy with a hard hat and a pick ax.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:55.180
Today mining requires high-end machinery and
world-class engineers.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:59.199
As you can imagine, these things are scarce
in a country as poor as Bolivia.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:05.940
If you wanted to create a competitive mining
industry in that country, without outside

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.460
help, you’d need decades.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.370
This is why it is so important to utilize
companies who have the technology, the tools,

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.020
and the staff to do the job.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:20.759
And this is why even Morales himself, unfriendly
to multinationals as he is, had to get out

00:05:20.759 --> 00:05:22.860
there and find investors.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:28.110
‘As soon as we have a big lithium industry,
Bolivia will set the lithium price for the

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:34.160
whole World’
‘I want to say to you, governments and private

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.530
companies, now you can join us’

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:44.580
OK, so what exactly is the problem here?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:48.349
Well… as we said before, Bolivian lithium
is owned by the state.

00:05:48.349 --> 00:05:51.250
This means that those companies who might
invest in the country, can only get a profit

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.069
from partnering with the government.

00:05:53.069 --> 00:05:59.719
And from that profit, they must pay a special
mining tax that goes up to 37.5%, which is,

00:05:59.719 --> 00:06:01.970
by far, the largest in the region…

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.210
And if this was not enough, according to the
World Bank, Bolivia ranks among the 50 countries

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.349
where it’s hardest to do business.

00:06:08.349 --> 00:06:11.379
They rank at about the same level as Sierra
Leone...

00:06:11.379 --> 00:06:15.150
Now, let’s say that you wanted to invest
in lithium!

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:20.319
Fancy investing in Bolivia, or maybe you might
prefer one of those other countries.

00:06:20.319 --> 00:06:21.699
Maybe.

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:26.289
This explains why, at this moment, Bolivia,
while it is the country with the biggest lithium

00:06:26.289 --> 00:06:29.570
resources, it is also the country that is
exploiting them the least.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:34.699
If you pay attention to the chart here, you
will see that today, the leader of the lithium

00:06:34.699 --> 00:06:40.029
race is AUSTRALIA.

00:06:40.029 --> 00:06:44.570
This is surprising because the resources of
this country are 4 times smaller than those

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.570
of Bolivia.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.749
Plus, Australian salaries are six times higher
than Bolivian ones.

00:06:48.749 --> 00:06:54.349
So, as you can see, this is not a matter of
low paid jobs or natural wealth- &nbsp;but, simply,

00:06:54.349 --> 00:06:57.139
good and bad economic policies.

00:06:57.139 --> 00:07:00.150
But hold on a minute, because this is not
the only problem...

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.770
Don’t forget that Evo Morales’s dream
for Bolivia is that it becomes a manufacturing

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.919
leader in the lithium battery industry.

00:07:06.919 --> 00:07:07.919
But…

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:08.919
well…

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:14.029
how exactly can they achieve this without
foreign companies setting up inside the country?

00:07:14.029 --> 00:07:20.770
Alright, alright, yes, the government can
set up its own factory.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:21.919
Great!

00:07:21.919 --> 00:07:26.729
But technology, patents and the skills needed
are held by companies like Panasonic, Samsung

00:07:26.729 --> 00:07:28.039
or Tesla.

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:32.689
Without these, Bolivia would need decades
of research in order to be competitive on

00:07:32.689 --> 00:07:34.099
the international market.

00:07:34.099 --> 00:07:36.999
Alright, so we mentioned Chile earlier…

00:07:36.999 --> 00:07:42.999
Well, what’s going on over there?

00:07:42.999 --> 00:07:45.749
CHILE FOLLOWS IN THE STEPS OF BOLIVIA

00:07:45.749 --> 00:07:49.749
For years, Chile has been known as something
of a free market Disneyland.

00:07:49.749 --> 00:07:54.780
More precisly, their mining industry was one
of the freest in the entire world.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:58.539
We are talking about a country where the economy
relies heavily on copper mining.

00:07:58.539 --> 00:08:05.120
This is why, in the year 1981, PINOCHET’s
dictatorship passed the so-called MINING LAW,

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:10.580
that allowed private businesses to own the
100% of a mine.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:14.199
As you can imagine, this law kick-started
foreign investment in the country.

00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:19.340
Suddenly, lots of companies like the Australian
BHP BILLINGTON or the Swiss XTRATA came to

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.889
Chile.

00:08:20.889 --> 00:08:21.889
And yes…

00:08:21.889 --> 00:08:22.889
I know what you are thinking…

00:08:22.889 --> 00:08:26.350
all of these multinational corporations looted
the country and left it in poverty, right?

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:27.350
Right?

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.400
Well… you’re actually wrong.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:34.690
Of course, these Canadian, Swiss and Australian
companies came to extract the copper.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:41.839
But they also helped to finance lots of brand
new companies which employed Chilean workers

00:08:41.839 --> 00:08:43.889
and were headquartered in SANTIAGO.

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:47.290
Companies like MINERA ESCONDIDA or ANTOFAGASTA
MINING.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:52.300
In fact, thanks to this wave of investors,
Chile now has a world-class mining industry.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:57.220
Actually, many of the engineers that are now
needed in Bolivia, live in the best neighbourhoods

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.220
of Santiago.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:04.060
And this means that, Chile has been in a great
position to lead the white gold rush.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:10.100
Nonetheless, in 2016, Chilean President, Michelle
Bachelet, declared that lithium was a different

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:11.380
animal.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:18.060
‘We confirm the strategic condition of lithium,
which is property of all the Chilean people

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:21.570
and we will keep its state of non-concessible
material’

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:22.570
–Michelle Bachelet

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:25.350
In other words, the government of Chile is
following suit with Bolivia.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.500
But with a difference.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:32.730
In this case, the country already has the
technology and the staff to exploit its mineral

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.699
wealth in an efficient way.

00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:38.560
Of course, many of those companies who were
willing to invest in the country have lost

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:39.560
all the interest.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:43.310
But Chile has its own companies so it’s
not that much of a big deal.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:47.779
Besides, until 2014, the other countries of
this Lithium TRIANGLE, Argentina and Bolivia,

00:09:47.779 --> 00:09:51.810
were way worse places for investment.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:57.440
So… this is sort of a “in the land of
the blind, the one-eyed person is king”

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:58.440
situation…

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.720
Until now.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.670
Argentina has been the big surprise here.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:06.210
While Chile and Bolivia have nationalized
their lithium and have tried, badly, to scare

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:10.630
away foreign companies, Argentina, with MAURICIO
MACRI (MAU RITHIO MAKRI) as its president

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.660
is doing something rather different…

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:19.140
And they are now getting all the attention
from international investors.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.639
But we’re going to talk about that in upcoming
weeks, in a sort of second-part to this video.

00:10:23.639 --> 00:10:27.639
So if you don’t want to miss that, please
do be sure to subscribe to this channel!

00:10:27.639 --> 00:10:30.180
In the meantime, we have question for you…

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.540
Do you think both Bolivia and Chile can reap
the benefits of their lithium with these kind

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:35.540
of policies?

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:38.190
Or maybe Argentina will overshadow them?

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.630
You can leave me your answer on the comments
section below.

